place: set front: cores 2-3 aren't the process's (0-1, 4-7); skipped
place: set db: cores 12-15 aren't the process's (0-1, 4-7); skipped
place: role workers: 4 threads on 2 cores; they share them
place: role writer: cores 2 belong to an exclusive set; it floats
place: role reports: cores 2-3 belong to an exclusive set; it runs on 4-5
place: role reports: 3 threads cut to the code's most, 2
place: the exclusive sets hold every core the process may use (0-7): a role the file doesn't name, or whose cores they hold, floats on any core, theirs included
place: role hasher: incoming needs a thread on one core, and each runs on 4-7; it does nothing
place: role writer: incoming needs a thread on one core, and they float; it does nothing
place: role reports: incoming needs a thread on one core, and they float; it does nothing
place: this platform can't pin threads: every thread floats
place: role workers: incoming needs a pinned thread; it does nothing here
